# Cloudflare Pages response headers (copied to dist/ by scripts/build.mjs).
#
# Pages, scripts and styles are checked with the server on every visit
# (Cache-Control: no-cache): the browser and Cloudflare may keep a copy, but
# ask first whether it changed, so a new deploy shows up on the next load and
# an unchanged file costs a quick "304 Not Modified". This is what keeps the
# owner dashboard (/admin/) and the planner from running last week's code.
#
# Not listed: /api/*. Pages Functions set their own headers and _headers never
# applies to them. Images, fonts and icons keep Cloudflare's defaults. The
# service worker (sw.js) keeps its own copy of the planner for offline use and
# goes to the network first, so the installed app still opens offline.
#
# One rule per address: when two rules match, Pages joins their values, so
# the page addresses below are exact and every file is covered by its type.
# tests/cache-headers.test.js checks that every page and file of the site is matched once.

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/admin/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/welcome/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/welcome/thanks/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/welcome/partners/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/legal/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/legal/privacy/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/legal/terms/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/legal/cookies/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
